# SwiftFormat — TokenMon
# Companion to SwiftLint: enforces *formatting* consistency (SwiftLint = rules).
# Strategy: keep the default rule set but disable the rules that conflict with
# this codebase's documented style (see .swiftlint.yml — long files, accepted
# force-unwraps in tests, spacing/wrapping preferences). This establishes a
# GREEN baseline on the current code; the enabled rules catch drift going forward.
# Tightening further (indent, redundantSelf, spaceAroundOperators, wrap* bodies)
# requires a one-time reformat — adopt deliberately, not as a drive-by.

--swiftversion 5.10
--exclude build,dist,.build,DerivedData

# Rules that would reformat the whole codebase / conflict with project style:
--disable \
  blankLinesBetweenScopes, \
  conditionalAssignment, \
  consecutiveSpaces, \
  docComments, \
  hoistTry, \
  indent, \
  noForceUnwrapInTests, \
  numberFormatting, \
  redundantClosure, \
  redundantMemberwiseInit, \
  redundantReturn, \
  redundantSelf, \
  redundantStaticSelf, \
  redundantThrows, \
  redundantType, \
  redundantVariable, \
  redundantViewBuilder, \
  spaceAroundOperators, \
  trailingCommas, \
  unusedArguments, \
  andOperator, \
  wrapFunctionBodies, \
  wrapIfStatementBodies, \
  wrapLoopBodies, \
  wrapMultilineStatementBraces, \
  wrapPropertyBodies
